@startuml
title Domain separation in FIPS 202: one permutation, six modes
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam ArrowColor #7A5BB5
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  BorderColor #7A5BB5
}

rectangle "Message M" as M #EDE0FA

rectangle "SHA3-224/256/384/512\nsuffix 01  ->  0x06\nc = 2d" as H
rectangle "SHAKE128 / SHAKE256\nsuffix 1111  ->  0x1F\nc = 256 / 512" as SH
rectangle "RawSHAKE128 / 256\nsuffix 11  ->  0x07" as RS
rectangle "cSHAKE (SP 800-185)\nsuffix 00  ->  0x04" as CS
rectangle "Original Keccak\n(Ethereum keccak256)\nno suffix  ->  0x01" as KE #FDEEEE

rectangle "pad10*1 to a multiple of the rate" as PAD #EDE0FA
rectangle "KECCAK-p[1600, 24]\nthe same permutation for every mode" as F #C9B3E8

M --> H
M --> SH
M --> RS
M --> CS
M --> KE
H --> PAD
SH --> PAD
RS --> PAD
CS --> PAD
KE --> PAD
PAD --> F

note right of KE
  Not part of FIPS 202. The competition
  submission appended no suffix, so
  keccak256 and SHA3-256 return different
  digests for the same input.
end note
@enduml
